From c9684fe8d0344f70a4b35ae0cda0920487bcd34c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:57:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/35] nx2: passthrough backend: hardware acquires
 (EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_HWACQ)

Sole mode: an acquire the host work submitted so far meets is left to the host channel and the front parses
on, instead of a host round trip through Eglantine per hop. The translator promises each semaphore write it
submits (QMD releases and reductions, SEM_EXECUTE, SEMAPHORE_D, report releases); the entry is translated up
to the acquire first, so a dispatch's own +1 just before counts. A passed fence (WFI after promised writes)
means memory holds them, so per-frame resets the translator does not see are followed. Every kept acquire's
release was submitted earlier: no host wait cycle, drains always finish. HWACQ=2 compares the entries the
front parsed ahead with memory once the acquire passes (MKW: 20 of 1.87M changed, GPU-culled parameters the
host reads again anyway).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
